{
 "language": "en",
 "duration": 117.867,
 "segments": [
  {
   "t0": 0.0,
   "t1": 1.18,
   "text": "Tonight, the moon disappears."
  },
  {
   "t0": 2.34,
   "t1": 2.52,
   "text": "Gone."
  },
  {
   "t0": 3.36,
   "t1": 4.18,
   "text": "What happens to us?"
  },
  {
   "t0": 5.08,
   "t1": 6.34,
   "text": "I'll answer that at the very end,"
  },
  {
   "t0": 6.82,
   "t1": 8.88,
   "text": "because first we need three smaller answers."
  },
  {
   "t0": 9.64,
   "t1": 11.6,
   "text": "Question one, would the oceans flood?"
  },
  {
   "t0": 12.68,
   "t1": 12.94,
   "text": "No."
  },
  {
   "t0": 13.6,
   "t1": 16.06,
   "text": "The moon's pull stretches the oceans into a bulge,"
  },
  {
   "t0": 16.5,
   "t1": 17.98,
   "text": "and that bulge is most of the tide."
  },
  {
   "t0": 18.58,
   "t1": 20.16,
   "text": "Without it, only the sun pulls."
  },
  {
   "t0": 21.0,
   "t1": 22.3,
   "text": "Tides shrink to about a third."
  },
  {
   "t0": 23.38,
   "t1": 25.74,
   "text": "Question two, would nights go black?"
  },
  {
   "t0": 26.66,
   "t1": 28.46,
   "text": "Every night becomes a new moon night,"
  },
  {
   "t0": 28.84,
   "t1": 30.96,
   "text": "and some animals tell time by moonlight."
  },
  {
   "t0": 31.86,
   "t1": 33.06,
   "text": "On the Great Barrier Reef,"
  },
  {
   "t0": 33.6,
   "t1": 35.12,
   "text": "corals release their eggs together"
  },
  {
   "t0": 35.12,
   "t1": 36.84,
   "text": "a few nights after a full moon."
  },
  {
   "t0": 37.52,
   "t1": 37.9,
   "text": "No moon."
  },
  {
   "t0": 38.54,
   "t1": 39.08,
   "text": "No calendar."
  },
  {
   "t0": 40.42,
   "t1": 43.32,
   "text": "Question three, would our days change?"
  },
  {
   "t0": 44.06,
   "t1": 45.52,
   "text": "Right now, the moon is a break."
  },
  {
   "t0": 46.0,
   "t1": 47.74,
   "text": "Its tides drag on Earth's spin,"
  },
  {
   "t0": 48.1,
   "t1": 50.16,
   "text": "so the day grows about two thousandths"
  },
  {
   "t0": 50.16,
   "t1": 51.94,
   "text": "of a second longer every century."
  },
  {
   "t0": 52.74,
   "t1": 54.98,
   "text": "Take the moon away, and the break is gone."
  },
  {
   "t0": 55.5,
   "t1": 57.4,
   "text": "The day stays 24 hours."
  },
  {
   "t0": 58.24,
   "t1": 61.24,
   "text": "Smaller tides, darker nights, the same day."
  },
  {
   "t0": 62.1,
   "t1": 63.28,
   "text": "That's fine?"
  },
  {
   "t0": 64.5,
   "t1": 67.52,
   "text": "Then why do scientists call the moon Earth's stabilizer?"
  },
  {
   "t0": 68.18,
   "t1": 69.7,
   "text": "Because Earth spins like a top,"
  },
  {
   "t0": 70.4,
   "t1": 71.88,
   "text": "tilted 23 and a half degrees."
  },
  {
   "t0": 72.94,
   "t1": 74.4,
   "text": "That tilt gives us seasons,"
  },
  {
   "t0": 74.94,
   "t1": 76.6,
   "text": "and the moon's pull holds it steady."
  },
  {
   "t0": 77.16,
   "t1": 80.04,
   "text": "It barely wobbles about one degree either way."
  },
  {
   "t0": 80.76,
   "t1": 82.64,
   "text": "Without the moon, the tilt can drift."
  },
  {
   "t0": 83.16,
   "t1": 85.16,
   "text": "One famous study found it could swing"
  },
  {
   "t0": 85.16,
   "t1": 87.14,
   "text": "from zero to 85 degrees."
  },
  {
   "t0": 88.12,
   "t1": 90.66,
   "text": "Newer studies say less, but still tens of degrees"
  },
  {
   "t0": 91.06,
   "t1": 92.46,
   "text": "over millions of years."
  },
  {
   "t0": 93.08,
   "t1": 95.18,
   "text": "At zero, no seasons at all."
  },
  {
   "t0": 95.66,
   "t1": 99.44,
   "text": "At 85, one pole faces the sun for half a year."
  },
  {
   "t0": 100.28,
   "t1": 102.44,
   "text": "Endless day, then endless night."
  },
  {
   "t0": 103.36,
   "t1": 105.38,
   "text": "So what happens if the moon vanishes tonight?"
  },
  {
   "t0": 106.02,
   "t1": 107.58,
   "text": "Tonight, almost nothing."
  },
  {
   "t0": 108.1,
   "t1": 109.68,
   "text": "But our far future grandchildren"
  },
  {
   "t0": 109.68,
   "t1": 112.4,
   "text": "would live on a planet that slowly forgets its seasons."
  },
  {
   "t0": 113.2,
   "t1": 115.26,
   "text": "Next, what if Earth stops spinning?"
  }
 ],
